 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "sentences is a non-empty list of sentences, each a sequence of words (runs of non-space printable ASCII) separated by single spaces, and maxWidth is a positive integer. Level 2 (inferred extension): each sentence is wrapped greedily into lines of at most maxWidth characters (a line holds as many words as fit, separated by single spaces; a word longer than maxWidth sits alone on its line). The inner width is the length of the longest wrapped line over all sentences, and each sentence forms one box holding its wrapped lines, left-aligned. Each box is a top border \"+\" followed by inner-width \"-\" characters and \"+\", then one content line per box line made of \"|\", the line padded on the right with spaces to the inner width, and \"|\", then a bottom border equal to the top. Boxes are listed one after another, each with its own borders. Return the list of output lines.",
  "provenance": [
   {
    "repository": "gamma",
